// GXV_HRW_WARP_DEPTH: 0 rotation only (every point at infinity); 1 depth-aware (the snapshot carries the first picture's depth); 2 (warp32 PATCH6) FOCUS PLANE: no depth
// snapshot, the whole picture is re-projected as one plane at the player's distance from the camera (the player's centre through the second picture's view matrix:
// port_hrw_player, GameScene.cpp), so what the follow camera keeps on the screen stays where a true redraw has it, the camera's rotation stays exact, and only scenery far
// from that distance is off by the camera's sideways move. GXV_HRW_WARP_FOCUS_LOCK=0|1 (default 1): 1 = the plane is moved so that the PLAYER'S CENTRE lands exactly where
// the second picture's camera sees it (his own move between the two turns included: the translation used is t = pB - R pA instead of the camera's); 0 = the plane is the
// still world at his distance (right for the ground under him, wrong for him by his own move). No player (a demo, no actor): rotation only, counted.
// (pace33 PATCH6: the mode in force is latched: the environment's value at first use, then a stage row's `warp_depth` at each stage's apply (StageApplied, below: a stage load, behind the
//  covered screen). It never changes between two pictures of a pair or inside a stage.)
std::atomic<int> g_depthMode{-1};
int DepthEnv() {
    int v = g_depthMode.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
    if (v < 0) {
        v = static_cast<int>(std::clamp<long>(EnvInt("GXV_HRW_WARP_DEPTH", 0), 0, 4));
        g_depthMode.store(v, std::memory_order_relaxed);
    }
    return v;
}
// 4 (warp32 PATCH11) ROTATION + PLAYER BOX: the scene rotation only (mode 0: no depth snapshot, one read a pixel), then the player's box as in mode 3 (the locked focus
// plane, same GXV_HRW_WARP_BOX_R / _FEATHER). Measured reason (c115): the follow camera's own translation is a few units a pair (1-2 px of parallax), so rotation only is
// nearly exact for the scene; the player's 6-8 px shiver is his own move, which only the lock takes out. No player: mode 0.
// (warp36, 14 Nov: "a few units" holds for a walk; while he RUNS the console logs have 11-18 units a pair (2892b), 5-10 px at his distance and 28 px at 300 units:
//  the owner's "double path". GXV_HRW36_PLANE re-projects the ground under him with the camera's move, GXV_HRW36_BOX shapes his box: see PlaneEnv / BoxEnv below.)
// 3 (warp32 PATCH9) HYBRID: the scene as mode 1 (the depth snapshot), then the player's box (his centre as B's camera sees it, GXV_HRW_WARP_BOX_R game units around it,
